Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a blend rolling on an edge of a face narrower than its radius
rolls on along that edge's line or circle past the edge's vertex on the
face at the end, at one end of the stripe or at both, and vanishes where
the narrow face ends in the spine's vertex (mitcad#343).

The cases: the walls of a notch 1 wide, strips 0.06 high on average
between the notch's floor (a cone) and its tongue, their edges with the
floor rounded with 0.86. The ball touches the floor and rolls on the
wall's far edge, a circle round the bar's axis (0342's RolledOnProlongedEdge
took lines only). At an end where the wall's far edge reaches a face W
that also holds the spine's end vertex, the files' roundings roll the ball
on along the circle and W cuts them; where the wall narrows to the spine's
vertex (its far edge running into it), the rounding ends in a point there.
OCCT's walk past the edge's vertex on W, rolling on W's edge with the wall,
failed, and the whole stripe with it; where the stripe started rolling on
the edge at such a vertex, RolledOnProlongedEdge took that piece for the
one rolling on the edge to be prolonged and found no face at the end.

- ChFi3d_RolledToFaceAtEnd: whether a piece rolling on an edge Er ends with
  that contact at Er's vertex A, A and the spine's end vertex on one face
  W other than the blend's faces and Er's.
- PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine: a walk rolling on an edge that fails past
  such an end stops there (the stripe is not invalidated).
- RolledOnProlongedEdge takes as P only a piece rolling on an edge with no
  vertex at the spine's ends, and Er a line or a circle (prolonged by the
  angle of the length, ChFi3d_RolledEdgeProlonged; the strip of B's surface
  beside it bounded by the curve offset towards B, ChFi3d_StripBeside-
  RolledEdge, shared with:).
- RolledOnProlongedEdgeAtEnd (where RolledOnProlongedEdge does not apply):
  the piece at one end of the stripe rolling on Er up to such an A, short
  of the spine's end (a piece ending at the spine's end, its section there
  in W, is left as it is: 0331's ball rolling on a line along the whole
  spine), is walked again from its other end, rolling on Er's line or
  circle past A up to the guide's end, and replaces it; its face is generated by the spine's edges
  the old one was. The corner at the spine's vertex cuts it by W from A
  (ChFi3d_RolledPastEdgeVertex, 0342).
- PerformFilletOnVertex: an end whose blend rolls on an edge that runs into
  the corner's vertex, with that contact at the vertex
  (ChFi3d_RolledIntoEndVertex), is put at the vertex within two hundredths
  of the radius, as a vanishing end (0902).

Upstream: new.

